VeridianOS: fix ConsoleKit seat discovery (QVariant::type(), "ao" reply)

GCC reported -Wdeprecated-declarations for QVariant::type() in
Authority::Private::init() (core/polkitqt1-authority.cpp), in the
ConsoleKit seat discovery, which never connected any seat:

- QVariant::type() reports every user type as QVariant::UserType (Qt 5
  and Qt 6 alike), so comparing it with qMetaTypeId<QDBusArgument>() was
  never true, and arg.toStringList() is empty for a QDBusArgument.
- Even with a matching check, the GetSeats reply is an array of object
  paths ("ao"), which QtDBus does not demarshall into a QStringList.

The check now compares QVariant::userType() and the reply is read as a
list of QDBusObjectPath, so DeviceAdded/Removed, SessionAdded/Removed
and ActiveSessionChanged of the seats present at startup are connected.
Only systems running ConsoleKit reach this code. Prepared for upstream
(invent.kde.org/libraries/polkit-qt-1, tested there with a fake
ConsoleKit on a private bus).

--- a/core/polkitqt1-authority.cpp
+++ b/core/polkitqt1-authority.cpp
@@ -229,8 +229,13 @@ void Authority::Private::init()
         // this method returns a list with present seats
         QStringList seats;
         QVariant arg = reply.arguments()[0];
-        if (arg.type() == qMetaTypeId<QDBusArgument>()) {
-            arg.value<QDBusArgument>() >> seats;
+        if (arg.userType() == qMetaTypeId<QDBusArgument>()) {
+            // the seats are object paths ("ao"), which do not demarshall into a QStringList
+            QList<QDBusObjectPath> seatPaths;
+            arg.value<QDBusArgument>() >> seatPaths;
+            Q_FOREACH(const QDBusObjectPath &seatPath, seatPaths) {
+                seats << seatPath.path();
+            }
         } else {
             seats = arg.toStringList();
         }
